/// REFUSE: Type mismatch!
///
/// Storing a wrongly typed element in an annotated collection -- issue #14.
/// The checker knows this argument is a String and does not look, so the
/// program runs and L[0] comes back a String.
///
/// ⚠️ This is the file that could not exist in the parent directory.  A static
/// check that fires produces NO observable behaviour except the program failing
/// to run, so no passing test block can assert it.  The whole reason the
/// refusal harness was built.
///
begin
    var Items : List of Integer := [];

    Items.Add (Str ('not an integer'));

    WriteLn (Str (Items[0]));
end
